SUMMARY:Deadline: GLINA3: Open Call for a Collaborator Working with Type\, 
 Language and Visual Systems
DESCRIPTION:GLINA3 is an Amsterdam clay 3D printing and digital design stud
 io\, and it is looking for one collaborator to join a new research project
  at the intersection of typography\, language\, technology and material cu
 lture. They want an artist\, writer\, poet\, anthropologist or artistic re
 searcher whose existing practice already engages with type design\, typogr
 aphy\, writing systems\, visual language\, fonts and letterforms\, languag
 e technologies\, or the tools that shape how language is produced\, read o
 r translated. This is an unusually good fit for anyone working on the mach
 ine-readable side of language: the brief explicitly names language technol
 ogies and translation tooling alongside classical type design. ELIGIBILITY
 : individual practitioners with demonstrable work in one or more of the li
 sted areas. HOW TO APPLY: the studio asks for relevant work\, research\, p
 ublications or projects connected to type\, fonts\, writing systems\, visu
 al language or the tools that shape them\, and nothing else. Because the d
 eadline is tight they say Instagram DM is the fastest route\; you can also
  email a short introduction and one relevant project to office@glina3.nl. 
 NOTE: the fee is confirmed only if the project's own funding comes through
 \, so clarify terms before committing time.\n\nOrganisation: GLINA3\nLocat
 ion: Amsterdam\, Netherlands (studio is Amsterdam-based\; collaboration te
 rms not specified)\nAward: Paid collaboration. The studio states the fee w
 ill be confirmed upon successful funding\, so the amount is contingent and
  not published up front. No application fee.\nDuration: New collaborative 
 research project\, length not specified\n\nMore: https://www.instagram.com
 /p/Dbse-4jDNj5/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.instagram.com/p/Dbse-4jDNj5/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Amsterdam\, Netherlands (studio is Amsterdam-based\; collaboration
  terms not specified)
